<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peace of Vervins</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1598">1598</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Treaty of Vervins · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-wars-of-religion">French Wars of Religion</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Peace of Vervins was signed on 2 May 1598 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-france">Henry IV of France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-spain">Philip II of Spain</a>, ending the war <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> had waged in support of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholic-league">Catholic League</a>. Spain returned Calais and other towns it had taken in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, restoring the frontiers of 1559. Together with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edict-of-nantes">Edict of Nantes</a>, issued the same spring, it ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-wars-of-religion">French Wars of Religion</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peace-of-vervins.jpg" alt="Peace of Vervins" width="320" height="199" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gillot Saint-Evre · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Paix_de_Vervins_par_Gillot_Saint-Evre.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
